1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:02,310
(Priya:)And for years,
everyone in my family

2
00:00:02,310 --> 00:00:05,380
was convinced that he was
the clarinet enthusiast.

3
00:00:07,180 --> 00:00:09,130
(Priya:)Hmm. What's that
piece of tape?

4
00:00:09,130 --> 00:00:12,920
(Leonard:)Oh, that one doesn't
apply to you. You sit.

5
00:00:14,150 --> 00:00:16,650
(Sheldon:)Hey.
Hey. How's it going?

6
00:00:16,660 --> 00:00:18,790
(Leonard:)Not too bad. Did you hear
about Howard and Bernadette?

7
00:00:18,790 --> 00:00:20,760
'Course I heard about it.
How did you hear about it?

8
00:00:20,760 --> 00:00:22,590
(Penny:)I heard about it
from Sheldon.

9
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:24,650
(Leonard:)He got it from Amy.
Oh, damn it.

10
00:00:24,650 --> 00:00:26,600
(Penny:)I told Amy that in the
strictest confidence.

11
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:29,770
(Penny:)Boy, some people are
such blabbermouths.

12
00:00:29,770 --> 00:00:31,190
(Penny:)Well, whatever.

13
00:00:31,190 --> 00:00:32,570
(Penny:)I'm sure Bernadette
can do better.

14
00:00:32,570 --> 00:00:36,140
(Leonard:)Do you think a sexually ambivalent
Indian astrophysicist

15
00:00:36,140 --> 00:00:38,830
(Leonard:)with selective mutism
and alcohol issues is better than

16
00:00:38,830 --> 00:00:42,200
(Leonard:)a hundred-pound Jewish guy
who lives with his mom?

17
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:44,750
(Penny:)You are kidding.
Raj likes Bernadette?

18
00:00:44,750 --> 00:00:48,340
I didn't say Raj.
Who said Raj?

19
00:00:48,750 --> 00:00:50,090
(Penny:)Okay, give.

20
00:00:50,090 --> 00:00:51,520
(Penny:)How do you know?
Did he tell you?

21
00:00:51,520 --> 00:00:53,870
(Dr. Brian Greene:)No.
Well, then who?

22
00:00:53,880 --> 00:00:56,040
(Leonard:)I can't say...

23
00:00:56,050 --> 00:00:59,460
(Penny:)Priya told you.
What a little gossip.

